''Objectives:'' Build and analyze a Mandarin subject–verb–object clause.


! First sentences

Start with [[Grammar/SVO Word Order]]. These are ''structural'' examples, not a request to memorize disconnected words.

|!Hanzi|!Pinyin|!Meaning|
|我学中文。|Wǒ xué Zhōngwén.|I study Chinese.|
|他吃饭。|Tā chī fàn.|He eats / has a meal.|
|师父教弟子剑法。|Shīfu jiāo dìzǐ jiànfǎ.|The master teaches the disciple sword techniques.|

! Analyze
# Identify the predicate in each sentence.
# Why is the third example not merely a one-object clause?
# Build a new sentence with [[Vocabulary/我]] and [[Vocabulary/吃]].

''Next:'' [[Lesson/02 Questions and Negation]]; [[Exercise/01 Clause Analysis]].


